1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:08,440
Slide 23 reveals the "SPARK OS DIRECTORY SETUP: Recommended project repository structure for your avatar."

2
00:00:09,340 --> 00:00:16,839
Look at the four clean directories displayed on screen: First, `agents/` stores specialized agent definitions.

3
00:00:16,839 --> 00:00:21,338
Second, `core/` contains the event loop and Gemini API connectors.

4
00:00:21,338 --> 00:00:25,360
Third, `logs/` maintains encrypted JSONL execution history.

5
00:00:25,360 --> 00:00:30,270
And fourth, `config/` holds environment variables and OAuth credentials.

6
00:00:31,170 --> 00:00:37,423
Notice our strict security rule: never commit `.env` or API keys to GitHub.

7
00:00:37,423 --> 00:00:43,510
All secrets must remain strictly isolated in local environment variables.

8
00:00:44,410 --> 00:00:51,862
In our starter repo, we provide a `.env.example` file that shows the required keys without exposing any production secrets.

9
00:00:51,862 --> 00:00:58,830
We also provide automated git pre-commit hooks that scan for accidental credential leaks before any code is pushed.

10
00:00:59,730 --> 00:01:06,160
Clean directory architecture ensures maintainability as your agent system expands throughout the semester.

